From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: syscall 435 has to answer something other than nosys

Two files, one decision, and they have to move together.

`bsd/kern/syscalls.master:653` chooses what syscall 435 *is*:

```
#if CONFIG_EMBEDDED || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
435  AUE_NULL  ALL  { int pid_hibernate(int pid); }
#else
435  AUE_NULL  ALL  { int nosys(void); }
#endif
```

`CONFIG_EMBEDDED` is a `defopt` in `config/MASTER` and this build does not set
it - `config/MASTER.arm64.milanf` is byte-identical to `MASTER.arm64.sweet`
apart from its header comment, and neither enables it. So on milanf, today,
syscall 435 is `nosys`, and `nosys` raises SIGSYS.

What calls it, from the comment already sitting above the function: *the iOS
userland runs on the macOS config, SpringBoard calls `pid_hibernate` when an app
leaves the foreground, and `nosys` (SIGSYS) killed it.* That is not a guess about
what might happen on milanf - it is what happened on sweet, recorded in the tree
by whoever fixed it there, with the same userland and the same syscall number.
Milanf inherits the bug and would inherit the diagnosis for free if anyone
remembered to look.

The other half is `bsd/vm/vm_unix.c:1758`, where the function itself lives:

```
#if !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
```

`XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX` is 1 for this build (`makedefs/MakeInc.def:72`), so on milanf
both sides are false and `pid_hibernate` is not compiled at all. This is the one
site in the inventory where widening *changes* which arm the board takes rather
than just adding a feature, which is why it was parked for a read instead of being
swept up with the mechanical ones - and the read says the change is the point.

Widening the master alone would produce `_pid_hibernate`, undefined, at link.
Widening `vm_unix.c` alone would compile a function nothing references. So both,
in one patch, is the only arrangement that is either correct or buildable.

What the function does on this board: nothing, by design. `CONFIG_FREEZE` is off
(also a `defopt`, also unset here), so the body is

```c
#ifndef CONFIG_FREEZE
#pragma unused(pid)
#else
        ...
#endif /* CONFIG_FREEZE */
        if (targetproc != PROC_NULL) {
                proc_rele(targetproc);
        }
        *ret = error;
        return error;          /* error == 0 */
```

which is exactly iOS with the freezer disabled: report success, freeze nothing.
The point is not the freezing. The point is that 435 stops raising SIGSYS in the
process that called it.

Nothing is lost on the macOS side: the guard has no `#else`, so macOS never had
this function to begin with and still does not. Sweet compiles the same text it
did before - the guard is widened, not reordered. And no hardware is touched
anywhere in the patch, so the recipe that has held for 0086-0098 applies: same
config for both boards, only the board defines differ, therefore anything that
compiles for sweet compiles for milanf unless it touches sweet's hardware.

Verified without a compiler: fresh ci-tail (ci-art3 + 0086..0098), both gate lines
asserted at exactly one occurrence each, the closing `#endif` comment updated so
it does not lie about which boards are inside, the header comment reworded
board-neutrally, patch CR=0, both sources CR=0, 0086-0099 sequential apply clean.
Link unverified; CI in the morning.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/syscalls.master b/bsd/kern/syscalls.master
index 422873e..2680eb5 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/syscalls.master
+++ b/bsd/kern/syscalls.master
@@ -650,7 +650,7 @@
 432	AUE_NULL	ALL	{ int audit_session_port(au_asid_t asid, user_addr_t portnamep); }
 433	AUE_NULL	ALL	{ int pid_suspend(int pid); }
 434	AUE_NULL	ALL	{ int pid_resume(int pid); }
-#if CONFIG_EMBEDDED || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if CONFIG_EMBEDDED || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 435	AUE_NULL	ALL	{ int pid_hibernate(int pid); }
 #else
 435     AUE_NULL        ALL     { int nosys(void); }
diff --git a/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c b/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c
index bb4a5d8..ec57f14 100644
--- a/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c
+++ b/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c
@@ -1755,9 +1755,10 @@ out:
 	return error;
 }
 
-#if !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || \
+    defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 /*
- * SWEET runs the iOS userland on the macOS config: SpringBoard calls
+ * The iOS userland runs on the macOS config here: SpringBoard calls
  * pid_hibernate when an app leaves the foreground, and nosys (SIGSYS)
  * killed it. Without CONFIG_FREEZE this returns 0, as on iOS.
  */
@@ -1822,7 +1823,7 @@ out:
 	*ret = error;
 	return error;
 }
-#endif /* !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX || SWEET */
+#endif /* !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX || SWEET || MILANF */
 
 #if SOCKETS
 int
